Turnip's KGSL backend advertises VK_KHR_calibrated_timestamps but its
device_get_gpu_timestamp is UNREACHABLE. vkd3d-proton's GetClockCalibration then
fails with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, which Unreal Engine 5 reports as a fatal
"Out of video memory" at startup (Half Sword).
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1707,6 +1707,12 @@
 kgsl_device_get_gpu_timestamp(struct tu_device *dev, uint64_t *ts)
 {
-   UNREACHABLE("");
+   /* ponytail: the arch timer runs at the GPU always-on rate (19.2 MHz) but has
+    * its own epoch, so this calibrates rates and not GPU query values exactly.
+    * Good enough for engine profilers; read the CP always-on counter if a tool
+    * ever needs them aligned. */
+   uint64_t counter;
+   __asm__ volatile("isb; mrs %0, cntvct_el0" : "=r"(counter));
+   *ts = counter;
    return 0;
 }
 
